  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-01">Adding a type touches only `recordTemplates.ts` and the sections map: `RecordTemplateModal.tsx` keeps no entity-specific branch. Each section is one component under `components/record/sections/`, looked up by section id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-01">Section behaviour is moved, not rewritten: the code in `RecordDetailModal.tsx` (`uploadOverride` :383, `DocumentsSection` :399, `DocumentDownload` :427, `InvoicesSection` :477 with `INVOICE_COLUMNS` :367, `EventsAndTasksSection` :513, ServiceRequestActions wiring :681-694, RecordMessages wiring :701-706) moves into the section files with the same props, requests and texts. The `AccessLevel.ViewOnly` props at :524-525 move unchanged (task 006 removes them).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-05 / FR-07">Document's Download and Service Request's "Delete request" become `RecordCommandBar` actions with icons from `RECORD_ACTION_ICONS`; Download is visible only when the record has a usable parent and `hasFile !== false`; Delete request only when R3's requester check passes. A hidden action is not rendered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The message-send and recall holds still block paging and Close (`holdNavigation`); the deleted-service-request state and `onRecordDeleted` still work; `onSettled` still fires once per settled record (the deep link depends on it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / tests/CLAUDE.md spirit">Every behavioural assertion in the deleted/ported R3 test files is either ported to the template or listed in the task notes with the reason it no longer applies. Do not delete a test file before its replacement passes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050 / ADR-021">No new envelope; Fluent v9 tokens only; each section uses the template's section card (header via `HeaderToolbar` per design §6 where a section has header actions).</constraint>
  </constraints>

