  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">For each of the six types, the template renders exactly the FR-01 left and right sections in order (a test per type).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grid row click, `?record=` deep link, notification-bell item and intake success link each open the template on the right record (existing tests for those paths pass, ported where needed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Document: Download is a toolbar action, present when a parent link exists and `hasFile !== false`, absent otherwise; a failed download shows the R3 error text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Service request: "Delete request" is a toolbar action shown only to the requester; 204 shows the deleted state and calls `onRecordDeleted`; 409 `has_related_records` offers the recall post.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A message send or recall in flight holds paging and Close.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`RecordDetailModal.tsx` no longer exists and no source file imports it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every assertion from the retired/ported R3 tests is ported or listed as obsolete with a reason in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an entity with no template entry opens nothing and throws nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">typecheck, lint and the vitest suite pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-01; plan Risk R4. Consumers verified 2026-11-10: `RecordOpener.tsx:16` and `GridWidgetBody.tsx:49` import `RecordDetailModal`; test files referencing it or its test ids: RecordDetailModal, DetailDocumentsDelete, DetailEventsTodosRoots, DocumentDetail.hasFile, DocumentDownload, RecordMessages, RecordDeepLink, NotificationBell, NotificationBell.noInteraction, App.notificationBell, App.deepLinkSignIn (all under `src/client/external-spa/tests/`). `DocumentDownload` already honours `hasFile === false` (`RecordDetailModal.tsx:436`, R3 ISS-011), so part of #1886 is on master; task 023 covers the rest. Toolbar create actions (Upload, New message, Add to-do, Add event) are task 004; visibility is task 006.

Completion (2026-11-11): `components/record/sections/` holds one renderer per section id (Information, Documents, Files interim, Invoices, Messages, Tasks & events, Preview interim) behind `renderRecordSection`; `components/record/actions/` holds the toolbar action hosts (Download, Delete request) keyed by action id, so the modal stays entity-agnostic. RecordTemplateModal reads `/me` once per opening, holds browsing/Close/Refresh while a section or host is busy (Refresh hidden; a failed in-flight refresh is held until release: task 003 K1 decided), and refreshes every section. RecordOpener and GridWidgetBody open the template; a type with no template opens nothing (opener reports terminal). RecordDetailModal.tsx and its test deleted after the port (47/47 R3 cases ported; only title strings changed, by FR-02). ArchTest walk path re-pointed to InvoicesSection.tsx. Suite 1343 tests in 48 files (load timeouts in 14 auth files re-run green), typecheck and lint clean. Review: no open F-class; D-5 (tests outside typecheck) filed PENDING. Detail: notes/task-005-notes.md.
rework: none task 005</notes>

